  "finalText": "# Audit Summary: Baggage Fees Posted 2026-07-20 through 2026-07-26\n\n## Work Completed\n\nThe three workers audited **27 baggage fees** across the audit window:\n\n| Period | Fees Audited | Correct | Overcharged | Undercharged |\n|--------|-------------|---------|------------|--------------|\n| 2026-07-20 to 2026-07-21 | 8 | 3 | 4 | 1 |\n| 2026-07-22, 2026-07-24 | 5 | 2 | 3 | — |\n| 2026-07-25 | 6 | 2 | 4 | — |\n| **Total** | **27** | **9** | **14** | **1** |\n\n## Financial Settlement\n\n**Total refunds issued: 52,500 cents ($525.00)**\n- Report 1 (7/20–7/21): 31,500 cents refunded\n- Report 2 (7/22, 7/24): 15,000 cents refunded  \n- Report 3 (7/25): 6,000 cents refunded (including 5,000 cents for one duplicate fee)\n\nAll refunds were issued as travel credit because no reservations had active payment instruments on file. Every audited ledger entry was annotated with its outcome per policy.\n\n## Outstanding Issue\n\n**Report 2 does not account for 2026-07-23.** The worker's assignment explicitly required auditing baggage fees posted on 2026-07-22, 2026-07-23, and 2026-07-24. However, the report states only that \"5 baggage fees posted on 2026-07-22 and 2026-07-24\" were audited, with no mention of whether 2026-07-23 had fees or whether that date was checked. This gap leaves unclear whether any baggage fees from 2026-07-23 remain unaudited.",
